# Line endings are decided here rather than by whatever each contributor's Git happens to be
# configured with.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which checks the whole tree out as CRLF.
# `gofmt -l .` - the first thing `make gate-quick` runs - then reports every .go file in the
# repository as unformatted, including files that have been green in CI for months. The gate can
# never pass on Windows, so it hides the failures that are real, and a gate contributors learn to
# ignore has stopped being a gate.

# Normalise every text file in the repository and check it out as LF on every platform. Git
# detects binary content on its own and leaves it untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Spelled out for the types where LF is not a preference but a requirement: gofmt writes and
# expects LF, a CR breaks the shebang of a script run inside a container, and goose reads the
# migration files.
*.go  text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf

# The exception. There is no Windows script in the tree today; the entry exists so that adding
# one does not quietly produce a file its own interpreter mishandles.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
